      "text": "To find the real value of \\( v \\) for which \\(\\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10}\\) is a root of the quadratic equation \\(5x^2 + 21x + v = 0\\), we can substitute the root into the equation and solve for \\( v \\).\n\nGiven root: \\( x = \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\)\n\nSubstitute \\( x \\) into the quadratic equation:\n\n\\[ 5\\left(\\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right)^2 + 21\\left(\\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right) + v = 0 \\]\n\nFirst, simplify \\( \\left(\\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right)^2 \\):\n\n\\[ \\left(\\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right)^2 = \\frac{(-21 - \\sqrt{301})^2}{100} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{441 + 42\\sqrt{301} + 301}{100} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{742 + 42\\sqrt{301}}{100} \\]\n\nNow substitute this back into the equation:\n\n\\[ 5 \\cdot \\frac{742 + 42\\sqrt{301}}{100} + 21 \\cdot \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} + v = 0 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{5(742 + 42\\sqrt{301})}{100} + \\frac{21(-21 - \\sqrt{301})}{10} + v = 0 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{3710 + 210\\sqrt{301}}{100} + \\frac{-441 - 21\\sqrt{301}}{10} + v = 0 \\]\n\nConvert \\(\\frac{-441 - 21\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\) to a fraction with a denominator of 100:\n\n\\[ \\frac{-441 - 21\\sqrt{301}}{10} = \\frac{-4410 - 2100\\sqrt{301}}{100} \\]\n\nCombine the fractions:\n\n\\[ \\frac{3710 + 210\\sqrt{301} - 4410 - 2100\\sqrt{301}}{100} + v = 0 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{3710 - 4410 + 210\\sqrt{301} - 2100\\sqrt{301}}{100} + v = 0 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{-700 - 1890\\sqrt{301}}{100} + v = 0 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{-700}{100} + \\frac{-1890\\sqrt{301}}{100} + v = 0 \\]\n\\[ -7 - 18.9\\sqrt{301} + v = 0 \\]\n\nSolve for \\( v \\):\n\n\\[ v = 7 + 18.9\\sqrt{301} \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( v \\) is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{7 + 18.9\\sqrt{301}} \\]",
